==English==

===Etymology===
From the act of tying or even nailing a pigeon to a stool to act as a decoy for hunters.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|En-au-stool pigeon.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|originally}} A pigeon tied to a stool by a piece of twine, used as a decoy to entice free-flying birds to the ground to be shot or trapped.
# {{lb|en|slang|obsolete}} A decoy used in a crooked gambling game.
# {{lb|en|slang}} An [[informer]] to the authorities, especially one who gives up criminal associates.
#: {{syn|en|stoolie|stooly|Thesaurus:informant}}

